Z||000005||ancosta||03-24-2001||04:24 AM||||What mods have you done to your Fiero?<P>As an SVT Contour owner I was a little suprised that you hammered one that hard. I did a little reading at:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/topfiero/fiero.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/topfiero/fiero.txt</A> <P>And from what it says, a 3.4/140HP Fiero is about .5 seconds slower 0-60 than an SVT and .4 seconds slower than an average 1/4 mile time. Note that the official SVT spec will say a 15.7 1/4 mile run, but I have run 15.5 in my car with horrible launches, and a lot of guys are running 15 flat completely stock. (SVT says a Lighning has 380HP, which is another gross understatement)<P>I kinda resent that statment that an SVT Contour a 'rice car' - it is anything but that. The roots of this car (all CDW27 platform cars) go deep into Europe, where the the car was developed by Ford as their 1st 'world platform' car. Funny that the net result of this project is that even one of the plain 4-banger variants of this American car has suprisingly good road feel, braking and handling. I liken it to driving a VW in that regard. The SVT Contour takes the european heritage and blends in a lot of proven performance tricks such as extrude-honing of the heads/intake, larger intake hardware, increased compression, free-flow exhaust, larger/beefier suspension and brakes, as well as a pretty nice wheel package (though it should come on 17s OEM). The body modifications are all very tastefully done, if not understated. Our SVTs are the first production autos to use Extrude Honing as an OEM process, and in 98/99 (and I think 2000) our SVT Contours output the highest HP/liter ratios (80HP/liter, IIRC) for any domestic automobile.<P>Two things all SVT owners will agree on are that yes you do have to wind the engine to get places in the car, and the car overall is an extremely balanced machine. It isn't all 1/4 mile, or all handling, or all braking. As a result, it makes an excellent auto cross car. We have a lot of folks who do quite well against other proven AutoX cars, i.e. Type Rs. Some folks are also pushing over 250HP at the wheels with power adders such as forced induction or N20. I personally find it hard to believe that if both cars were stock, and both drivers were equally competent, that an 88 Fiero would smoke an SVT. Then again, we have ppl on contour.org who have smoked 'faster' cars, i.e. 5.0s pretty hard. I know it to be impossible for the Fiero to win if that race involved winding roads that the Fiero would come out on top (again being both stock and equal drivers). We should also keep in mind that the Fiero is at a disadvantage because the technology behind the car is 10 years older (and it was built by GM - opps that was a cheap shot!). Then again back in 86 we had the SVO Mustang which would have whooped an 86 Fiero pretty hard. Then again in 89 you guys had the 3.8L turbo Firebird, which was a really hot car, and would have smoked all 5.0 stangs off the factory floor.<P>While any vehichle can be riced out if put into the wrong hands, a stock SVT Contour is anything but rice - it is a car unlike any other domestic automobile. (you could say SHO, but the SVT Contour is much more balanced from the factory) Unfortunately, it has also gone the way of the Fiero.<P>Andrew<BR>99 SVT Contour<P>*** Ammendment ***<BR>Opps I did some reading it it does appear that a 3.4 is a custom engine for this car. A search on Google says that ppl are claiming low 14 second 1/4 mile times with this motor swap.<P>So, if you are running low 14's then you most definately could beat a stock SVT. However, if motor swaps are fair game, then you would be running against a 3L SVT, some of which are putting 250HP to the wheels, normally aspirated. This would be a very fair run against a similarly modded 3.4L Fiero. Granted, RWD and weight are always going to be advantages in favor of the Fiero. A more suitable competitor to the SVT Contour would probably be a Grand AM GT. We've raced enough of those to know what they're about  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by ancosta (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||03-24-2001||06:29 AM||||Im not sure if the SVT (Special Vehicle Team) is the same as the SHO (Super High Output)Taurus. <P>I had a guy that thought his SHO was the top dog of American cars, until I bent over his hood and sniffed it saying that I smell rice coming from underneath. The V8 in the SHO was designed by Yamaha (very well I have to admit) and I loved it even more when he muttered at me "You aren't supposed to know that..."||||reg||6
Z||000007||RTStabler51||03-24-2001||09:50 AM||||Actually the 89-95 Taurus SHO engine was all developed by Yamaha.  It was assembled and shipped complete from Japan.  As for the 96-99 3.4 V-8 SHO, if I remember correctly it was a joint effort between ford and Yamaha.    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B>Im not sure if the SVT (Special Vehicle Team) is the same as the SHO (Super High Output)Taurus. <P>I had a guy that thought his SHO was the top dog of American cars, until I bent over his hood and sniffed it saying that I smell rice coming from underneath. The V8 in the SHO was designed by Yamaha (very well I have to admit) and I loved it even more when he muttered at me "You aren't supposed to know that..."</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>------------------<BR>Ryan<BR><B>Thunderbird Moderator</B>       <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.islc.net/~shoman//Sig_files/image002.gif">  <BR>   <A HREF="http://www.islc.net/~shoman/Contour.htm" TARGET=_blank><BR><B>98.5 Silver Frost Contour SVT 5979/6535</A>             <BR><I>Born: May 15, 1998</I></B><P>  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/cwm2/piss2.gif[/IMG][IMG]http://www.gm.com/images/gmlogo.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by RTStabler51 (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||03-24-2001||10:01 AM||||Why Do people find this list come on and talk about how much better their car is? Some MR2 guys do it , there was a guy in O/T that did it with his 3000GTVR4??  <P>A properly set up Type R should whoop a Contour SVT @ an autocross. I have been around autocrossing for around 10 years now , I have been to the Divisionals , nationals ect (SCCA) and I have yet too see the SVT Contour beat a competitive Type R. <P>Contours have 64% of their weight on the front wheels..and weigh 3200Lbs , I don't really see how their well balanced. In contrast a Type R has 58% of it's weight on the front wheels and weighs 2700lbs<P>I used to work for Kennedy Ford in Oakville Ontario (SVT dealer)(among other places) The press pack I have here for the SVT says 7.8 Sec to 60 , 143 Mph Top speed. <P>I don't think it's impossible for a fiero to win on winding roads ..I think a well driven 88 formula would beat an SVT contour. It's better balanced all around, and it's suspension may be 12 years old , but it's still pretty advanced for todays technology..mate that with the fact the car is mid engined...<P>The SVO comment...also a little off as well had a post last week about a fellow who raced a SVO stang, I can attest to the comment being the former owner of a merkur with a few light mods to it's motor (turbo city boost valve , IC , ect)<P>People under estimate our little cars sooo much. <P>Don't get me wrong , I think ford has made leaps and bounds with the SVT program and I would love to have one in my garage, that combined with the new DEW98 platform the Lincoln,Jag S type and T Bird are built on have proved ford is a world leader in automobiles, and I love what J Mays is doing with design.<P><BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<P>TR MotoSports Typhoon Wheels 255/40/17" rear , 225/45/17 Front. 911 C2 spec Pirelli P Zero's, 11.25" vented Discs, willwood 4 piston calipers, Koni's , Big Bars , <BR>Carrera front springs , Ground Control coil overs mounted on Koni's rear , poly -urathaned ,Short shifter , Momo pedals , <BR>momo Shift knob , Pioneer DEH 6000 CD  , Sony Mobile 504X amp, No Cat, Accell Coil, Cold Air Induction. 4 point Harness, <P>Shown, Autocross'd,Tracked ..abused. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||KnightRyder31||03-24-2001||10:43 AM||||FORD...<BR>IF backwards,<BR>Driver Returns On Foot!!!!!<BR>Forwards,<BR>F'd Over Rebuilt Dodge!<BR>My friend and I blew a newer Rustang GT away last night!!! It made me smile <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<BR>And all we had was four banger!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||firstfiero||03-24-2001||11:12 AM||||    Nice kill man!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> After riding in my father in laws svt lightning I have to say that team at ford makes an incredible piece of machinery. 0-60 in 5.7 seconds is incredible for a truck. And the new model has added horses and cut that number down to 5.2! As they said on car and driver tv "Thats pretty good for a 3000 pd truck with the aerodynamics of a brick"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> anyway don't know much about the contours other then between that and the new svt focus I don't know which is more of a waste of time! <BR>      another thing...How the hell do these people keep finding us!! Nobody ever wants to believe they can be beat by are lowly fieros until their stairing at out tail lights!!  Oh well...The ricers can keep under estimating my se and I'll keep drilling them for it...<P>------------------<BR>'86 fiero Se<BR>    Todd<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!!||||reg||14
Z||000011||ancosta||03-24-2001||11:13 AM||||My original post wasn't to flame the Fiero. I just thought I'd put a non SVT-savvy ppl in the know that the SVT Contour is not a ricemobile, and that it uses a lot of proven technology to deliver some potent performance. If you go on contour.org or look at some MT articles, you will find that the SVT Contour will run 0-60 in 6.9 and do the 1/4 in close to 15 flat. (MMFF did a test in 98 where they got 15 flat in the 1/4)<P>I don't think that the SVT Contour and Fiero are similar enough of a car to really say one is better than the other. When it comes to subjective things like 1/4 mile, AutoX, etc. sure we could compare, but then it all comes down to mods...eventually you would have a northstar in the back of a Fiero, and a BTCC Mondeo...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I think the only real metrics for comparison are 1) which car kicks more ass stock, and 2) which car can kick more ass with a few mods. IIRC, the SVT Contour would be hands-down winner of 1), however 2) would certainly be open for debate.<P>As far as the guy who was beating TypeR, I think that would be davidz on the contour.org forum. Do a quick search and you should find some good stuff.<P>I agree they are doing something cool with the Jaguar X type. I just hope that it isn't too chintzy, and that it really can be a strong contender to the 3 series, a4, etc.<P>One other thing that us SVT ppl don't really like - how SVT basically abandoned all support for our Contours once they were put on the chopping block :/ They don't even mention our cars in their newsletters anymore, and even at that, we now have to pay to get them. I though that 22.5K should buy me a membership for at least that. Then again, why would we care if it doesn't even include our cars.<P>Andrew<BR>99 SVT<P>PS: On trolling forums: we get more than our share on contour.org, some of which are GM products that "bring excitement" (or something to that effect)<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Why Do people find this list come on and talk about how much better their car is? Some MR2 guys do it , there was a guy in O/T that did it with his 3000GTVR4??  <P>A properly set up Type R should whoop a Contour SVT @ an autocross. I have been around autocrossing for around 10 years now , I have been to the Divisionals , nationals ect (SCCA) and I have yet too see the SVT Contour beat a competitive Type R. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||03-24-2001||02:40 PM||||ancosta, I think I learned more about the Ford Contour in your first post then I ever have reading a C&D or Motor Trend article!  Very informative.  For the record I don't consider it flaming or anything, I think you represented your car well, unlike the 3000GT owner who was an a$$.  I for one welcome people like you since often times so many facts are misrepresented about cars other then the ones the forum is dedicated to.  It happens all the time with Fiero's, you hear everything from fiery death trap to those cars came stock with turbo's or what have you.  I have been on more then a few boards myself trying to set people straight.<P>I'm not calling <I>all</I> Contours rice.  I actually like them (and in general I hate Ford anythings), but this one was rice.  It had like 18" wheels (in ghetto chrome) and a ricer type exhaust.  It also had like some kind of hood with a scoop on it, I couldn't really tell since he was in my rearview most of the time and it was at night.  I don't really like to check out cars when I am going over 100 mph! hehe.  I would have stopped to talk but my street was up ahead.<P>Pertaining to the 3.4.  While it is not a stock engine offered in any Fiero, it is still a 60 degree V6 like the original 2.8.  Understandably you probably don't know this so I won't hold it against you, but with the 3.4 "swap" all you use is the block and the heads (which BTW are the same as stock 2.8 heads w/the exception of valve springs, I just used them because they were in better shape then my 2.8 heads).  So when you look at a 3.4 in a Fiero it will look just like a 2.8, since you retain the Fiero intake and manifolds, sensors etc. etc.  So while it technically is a swap its not like a 3800 swap or a N*. Just imagine it as a built Contour SVT motor I guess you could say.  Low 14s is maybe with a modded 3.4 (bored, ported heads) but I didn't have the money/time for that when I installed the 3.4 so it is stock internally, every mod I have is basically bolt on (msd, borla etc.)<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||14
Z||000013||cjbaldw||03-24-2001||02:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Well its no vtec prelude (hehe) but its my first kill of the year....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heh,<P>Good kill.  This is my first post to this board, so go easy on me guys...<P>I've been dead even with every VTEC Prelude I've raced yet, they are nutin special IMHO.  Regarding the Contour SVT in general (Yes...I own one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), I don't see why u guys r downing Ford so much.  I'm not really brand loyal to any car manufacturer.  I've owned Fords, Mazdas, Subarus and Hondas so far, they've all been good cars for me.  Comparing the SVT Contour, a four door front drive performance sedan, to a Fiero, a two door mid engined RWD sporty car, is like comparing apples to oranges, they are built for two very different purposes.<P>IMHO, the Fiero was a card GM played too early in the game, it was a car ahead of it's time in many respects, especially for GM's reputation/marketing strategies at the time it was built.  It's a shame the platform was killed off when it was.  A guy on my wife's side of the family used to own a GT Fiero, was a nice car.<P>What is up with the 3.4L engine swaps, what kinda performance do these cars put out, i.e 1/4's, 60ft, etc., after the swap?  How much $$$ to do the swap?<P>Most SVT Contours r running in the low 15's stock, low 15's to high 14's with NA mods.  Vortech recently released an SC kit for the 2.5L Duratec engines in general, which includes all V6 Contours and the SVT models.  We have a couple of guys running the new SC kit on their Contours over on contour.org (both normal V6 models and SVT V6's - yes, they r different), I think most people r kinda waiting to see how the engine holds up under FI before taking the plunge, I know I am since it's my daily driver right now.<P>Anyways, I'm paying off my 99 SVT next month and I'm looking at a 96 LT-4 Vette 6-spd as my weekend driver's car (yes, I might buy my first GM car!).<P>Later guys...<P><P>------------------<BR>Regards,<P>Craig J. Baldwin<BR>99 SVT Contour - Silver - #49/2760 - ES Front Motor Mount Inserts, Bosche +4's w/Magnecore 8.5mm Competition wires, RActive Racing Pedals, KKM Intake/Pro-M 75mm MAF||||reg||2
Z||000014||Trapps||03-24-2001||03:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KnightRyder31:<BR><B>FORD...<BR>IF backwards,<BR>Driver Returns On Foot!!!!!<BR>Forwards,<BR>F'd Over Rebuilt Dodge!<BR>My friend and I blew a newer Rustang GT away last night!!! It made me smile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<BR>And all we had was four banger!<P>I see you are in Michigan. Care to race?<P>Mark<BR>99 Contour<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Black88GT||03-24-2001||03:25 PM||||You have to expect ford bashing on a GM car board!  Go over to a mustang board and *mention* the word Corvette, and see what you get lol.  You know how people are, Fords Suck Chevy's suck Imports suck blah blah blah. <P>That would be cool, S/C Contour SVT.  Oh I was saying that vtec Prelude comment in a sarcastic way, there too heavy but I am sure someone has modded them insanely and ran like 11s or whatever.  <P>The 3.4 we use is from 93-95 Camaro's/Firebirds.  You can also use 3.4's from some minivans but they are hard to find from what I understand.   These 3.4's have cast iron heads so the output is around 160 hp and 215 lb ft. torque (some say more Hp with Fiero intake, how true that is I have no clue).  Newer 3.4s ("3400s") have better aluminum heads so there output is around 180 Hp.  I think Formula88 has a desktop dyno so he could give you Qtr. mile times for a stock 3.4, but most who do 3.4s have some mods to go along with it.  Stock Fiero's ran high 15s-low 16s with the 2.8 so I would imagine with the 3.4 it would be low 15s with no other mods.  The Fiero launches exceptionally well due to its design.  In fact the stock Formula has 0-30mph in 2.2 seconds which is equal to many exotic cars, I think the only car faster (stock) in the S/C MR2 made in '89 which was 2.0 seconds to 30.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||cjbaldw||03-24-2001||04:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>The 3.4 we use is from 93-95 Camaro's/Firebirds.  You can also use 3.4's from some minivans but they are hard to find from what I understand.   These 3.4's have cast iron heads so the output is around 160 hp and 215 lb ft. torque (some say more Hp with Fiero intake, how true that is I have no clue).  Newer 3.4s ("3400s") have better aluminum heads so there output is around 180 Hp.  I think Formula88 has a desktop dyno so he could give you Qtr. mile times for a stock 3.4, but most who do 3.4s have some mods to go along with it.  Stock Fiero's ran high 15s-low 16s with the 2.8 so I would imagine with the 3.4 it would be low 15s with no other mods.  The Fiero launches exceptionally well due to its design.  In fact the stock Formula has 0-30mph in 2.2 seconds which is equal to many exotic cars, I think the only car faster (stock) in the S/C MR2 made in '89 which was 2.0 seconds to 30.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Kewl swap info.  If the 3.4L swap is only running low 15's then I'm uncertain why you smoked the SVT so bad, r u running more mods/better times yourself?<P>The SVT model isn't really strong off the line for a few reasons.  One, 2.5L is a small displacement V6, generating 200HP/169TQ, and it is high revving, so it's not as easy to get a good launch especially in comparison to a 3.4L V6 w/215TQ.  Two, no LSD, bummer, which doesn't make launches from a stop any easier.  The SVT really excels at higher speeds, it's a touring sedan IMHO, over 100MPH the car really does well.  I wish these kinda speeds were legal here!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I see u live in Baltimore, I live about an hour north of you in Bear, DE, about a 1/2 hour south of Wilmington.  There's an LT4 Corvette at Glen Burnie Auto down your way, know anything about these guys?  I'm thinking of heading down there to take a look at the Vette...<P>------------------<BR>Regards,<P>Craig J. Baldwin<BR>99 SVT Contour - Silver - #49/2760 - ES Front Motor Mount Inserts, Bosche +4's w/Magnecore 8.5mm Competition wires, RActive Racing Pedals, KKM Intake/Pro-M 75mm MAF||||reg||12
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||03-24-2001||05:11 PM||||Transmission has a lot to do with it. the 4spd 85/86GT V6 cars seem to be the fastest stock fiero's. I have run a best of 6.54 sec to sixty with a bone stock 2.8 , no cat , cold air intake , short shift. This was on a GTEC , several different occasions I have turned mid 6's , with people in the car , without (Chris moore and Fierolisa have both been witness)<P>I have seen a few 3.4Fiero's with 4 and 5spd run High 14's stock ... even with terrible launches..<P>I have a few video's I need to convert to Avi , But I will soon . 3.4's and so on running the 1/4<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000018||Sleeper||03-24-2001||05:29 PM||||good job Black88GT, last year some dude(middle aged) in a SVT Contour started to f*ck with me on the road so i got into with him. the race was pretty equal on a 2 mile light to light street. the contour did did well on turns too, i was pretty impressed. though you proved me wrong you smoked him .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, J.E.T. super chip, MSD Blaster Coil, K&N filter and Optima Battery.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Black88GT||03-24-2001||05:36 PM||||Yes I have other mods to go along with the 3.4, ported exhaust manifolds, MSD-6AL with MSD coil, Borla exhaust, no cat., ported TB, port matched upper and lower intake manifolds.  That low 15 number is a bone stock heavier GT, I lighter SE model or Formula could probably pull off high 14s if driven right.<P>Hey I have some relatives in Delaware.  About the Corvette place, there are so many car dealerships in Glen Burnie its tough for me to remember.  I live about 15 min. from there.  Do they specialize in Vette's?  I know of this one place in Baltimore County that has a ton of vette's, about 30, only a few C5's mostly last year C4's, might be worth a look.  I could get the number for you if you wanted.<P>p.s. I just got done reading on the contour forum their replies, any of those chumps want to race, name the time and place.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||7
