Z||000022||fyerstarter||03-24-2001||11:25 PM||||Vtec Preludes are nothing big. Me and my friend beat one in his moms bone stock 87 Toyota Carolla FX16 Wagon!  And that's no bullshit. From a dead stop to about 90... twice. I mean it was close but we won both times. Talk about being underestimated in a race! :P Watch out for this little bastards on the street I tell ya, they are sleepers, with a 1.6L, 16 valve, twin-cam (I think the motor out of the MR2) redlining at 8 grand they are faster than my 87 GT with headers, intake, flowmaster and some minor valve work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Oh and to the guy who said he beat a newer Stang Gt in a 4 banger. Was this a 4 banger fiero? If so, who was driving the Stang? An 80 year old lady? Hmmm...sounds like some of the fish stories you hear over at speedmagazine.com :\||||reg||1
