Z||000028||Black88GT||03-25-2001||05:02 PM||||Yeah its funny how much they whine.  Sound more like Mustang owners to me.  They had me questioning if it was a real SVT (even though it had the right SVT badging) but when I saw the part on the site which talked about the bumper sag thing, I knew it was, because I am very observant and when I was behind him at the red light and he launched I got a good look at how is rear bumper was sagging, I thought it was repaired or something from a previous accident.<P>About that Corvette, maybe its just me but it seems like a high price for the mileage.  Whats the book value?  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000029||cjbaldw||03-25-2001||07:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>About that Corvette, maybe its just me but it seems like a high price for the mileage.  Whats the book value?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Depends, retail book value is $23695, but I'd only rate the car in fair condition, as it needs paint/sanding on the front bumper and some paint chips on the hood.  Fair trade in value is $14805.  He's asking $18995 for it, although he claims someone is buying it for $19995 on Wednesday.  I'll wait and see.  I'd pay $17500 for the car personally, no more than that.<P>Later...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Regards,<P>Craig J. Baldwin<BR>99 SVT Contour - Silver - #49/2760 - ES Front Motor Mount Inserts, Bosche +4's w/Magnecore 8.5mm Competition wires, RActive Racing Pedals, KKM Intake/Pro-M 75mm MAF||||reg||1
Z||000030||Trapps||03-25-2001||11:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KnightRyder31:<BR><B>Trapps, where in Michigan do you live?<BR>And since I don't have a working car right now, I won't be able to race...my friend will though.<BR>BTW, My friend's car is a Dodge Daytona Shelby series turbo 5-speed.<BR>I doubt you will win, but what the heck.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Detroit area. I mistakenly assumed in your first post that you blew away a 'Rustang GT' with a Fiero. I'm not here to start sh!t, just a true enthusiast who will race any car, win lose or draw. I'm up for racing your friends Daytona though. How about a trip to Milan?<P>Mark<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000031||Goody||03-26-2001||08:20 AM||||The first car I owned was an '85 Fiero 2M4 with a quad-4 swap that had been done by the previous owner.  She was a good car until that snowy day she ended up in the woods.  Ah well, hope her parts are doing well on my friends car.  I know that car was fast.  It was hellish fast for such a light, nimble car.  I was always impressed at how well that car would keep up with most things that came across it's path.<P>But you know what?  I own a Contour now.  I find this flame war funny, because I never thought it would happen.  I never thought I'd see the day when someone would claim to "Whup up" on an SVT Contour in ANY Pontiac that wasn't an F-body.  Granted, the GPGTP's are fast off the line, but try and keep up in the twisties... The GAGT?  Ha!  But a Fiero... Oh, I've just been looking for that race, because I knew it would definately be a race of skill, not of power and mods.<P>I find it really hard to believe that this person had 5 car lengths on an SVT, stock or not.  I've raced stock FGT's in my Contour and it's always been a close race, but at the high end of the scale (above 50mph) the 'Tour always wins out.  Off the line, yeah the Fiero's got some punch versus the CSVT, but I really find it hard to believe that he pulled away from him so easily in 3rd gear.  <P>As an aside, the "Screaming" you heard from the engine is the way it should sound.  The SVT has a 2.5 (not 2.8) litre DOHC V6 with a readline around 7000RPM (Higher with a chip), and puts out roughly 200HP at about 6300RPM.  It's one of the highest specific outputs of any stock, naturally aspirated engines out there, especially in it's price range.  It rumbles nicely at idle, but get it up into it's powerband and it wails.<P>Oh, and BTW, firstfiero... I drive through York once a month on my way to Lancaster, care to talk ****  after I whoop your ass?||||reg||7
Z||000032||KnightRyder31||03-26-2001||08:40 AM||||Trapps, I've haven't been there yet.<BR>So this could work, I've always been meaning to get down there. I'm sure my friend would like to go. Give my a date, and I'll check with him.||||reg||1
Z||000033||firstfiero||03-26-2001||10:37 AM||||   Kick my ass... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">....whats your beef with me? I think contours are ugly pieces of ****  and complete waste of the svt teams time. I also said I do respect the speed of an svt anything. That being said to each his own!If you like and enjoy driving your contour..good for you. I take crap for loving my fiero so much all the time! I know I'll take you off the line but like you said you have a lot of life in the powerband after 3rd an unfortunatly thats when the fiero shuts down. I'll race you for shits and giggles though. Hell I'll race anybody and be happy to talk to them afterwords win or lose. I'm not a ricer so I don't pull the old ricer fly by thing. <BR>    By the way I stand by what I said about people being imbarrased by loosing to a fiero. People don't understand or respect the car  until they actually get in one and drive it. <BR>    heres why I think I beat most of the kids on the street even when they have a faster car. A fiero (v6)  will take most cars off the line. People here that nice roaring engine go by see you get that quick 2 car length lead and shut down. They don't know what their racing so they don't realize that if they stay on it they'll reel us in. Just my oppionon but I think the fiero is one of the easiest cars to get clean start of the line with. It also doesn't hurt that these kids think that spinning your tires of the start is a good thing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>   <P>------------------<BR>'86 fiero Se<BR>    Todd<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!!||||reg||4
Z||000034||Black88GT||03-26-2001||11:53 AM||||OK maybe some of you Contour owners have a problem with reading comprehension, but lets try this again.<P><B>MY CAR IS NOT STOCK</B><P>Ok did it get through that time?  If I had a 2.8 GT and was saying I did this, I wouldn't believe me either.  I have raced a turbo eclipse on this same road before, and we came out almost dead even by the next light.  I don't feel like digging it up but its on the forum somewhere.  <P>About that Pontiac comment (no one would ever claim to whoop up on an SVT without an F-Body) Well right down the street from me is a street legal 11 second GTO, unless those Contours are running 11s then.  Also there are <I>PLENTY</I> of Fiero's out there that would take any SVT Contour.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||10
