Z||000041||Trapps||03-26-2001||11:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<B> Also there are <I>PLENTY</I> of<BR>Fiero's out there that would take any SVT Contour.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Again, just an<BR>enthusiast here, not trying to perpetuate sh!t, but that's a very bold<BR>statement! Let's all agree that there are some very fast and capable Fieros;<BR>and equally, some very fast and capable Contours. The typical trolling and<BR>flame wars on the CEG site are with groups who are into similar styles of<BR>cars (mid size, 4 doors, front engine, FWD). Here we have 2 completely<BR>different cars which may or may not live in the same performance envelope.<BR>Yes we can talk objectively about motor to motor, trans to trans, ¼ to ¼,<BR>top end to top end, but like most all comparisons, this is a subjective<BR>discussion from a total package standpoint. <P>I wouldn't call this a flame war, just two groups getting to know each other<BR>a little bit. I do have some history in the Fiero ; in 1986, while at<BR>Arizona State, I spun a classmates GT into a telephone pole. While it was a<BR>very fun car to drive, I was young and inexperienced - particularly with mid<BR>engine RWD. Please remember that  ALL groups have members who are logical<BR>and rational and open minded. At the same time, ALL groups have a percentage<BR>of members who are more emotional and perhaps less open minded (educated?).<BR>If you subscribe to the first description, bring on the discussion, debate<BR>and challenges to race. <P> I am benefiting from this thread. I didn't know there were options for the<BR>Fiero, at least what appear to be fairly common options. I see the odd V8<BR>stuffed in a Fiero on my routine drives up and down Woodward Ave, but I<BR>thought that to be the extreme exception. The Contour has been quite limited<BR>in after-market or performance options; that is changing though. The recent<BR>release of s/c and 3.0L versions is a big step up in performance for<BR>Contours. <P>I don't own just 'any' SVT Contour. I would be happy to participate in a<BR>meet or event with Fieros and Conoturs. Mabey a road race, Autocross, drag<BR>race, or just talk cars over a few beers. For those of you in the Detroit<BR>area,  a trip to Milan in late April would be fun. I'll post an invite and<BR>date here when I have it sorted out (and the weather improves :-) ).<P>Mark<BR>1999 Contour SVT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1204400&a=8883688&p=44521924"> ||||reg||1
Z||000042||Terrybogin||03-27-2001||12:17 AM||||Very tasty Contour Uncle Ben.||||reg||1
