Z||000044||Trapps||03-27-2001||12:27 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>      Took me a second...but I think you were saying rice. At least he doesn't have any stickers or a 3 tiered wing...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you saying my car is Rice? If so why? I'm not a fan of rice and I don't think mine is,  but our definitions may vary.........<P>Mark<P><p>[This message has been edited by Trapps (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000045||Standard||03-27-2001||02:34 AM||||I think he's trying to say.. "do you have any mods other than rims and exhaust?"...<P>I never have and never will be a fan of bubbly cars, or 4 door cars for that matter.  The contour is one of those, but I'm not saying it's slow or can't handle or whatever, it's just not what I like...  IMHO a "family car" like that just can't look good.  not flaming you, just expressing my opinion.<P>And there is the fact that you can have a fully built Fiero (coilovers f&r, poly all around, big brakes, rims, built v6/v8 etc) for less than the cost of a contour, if you know what you're doing.  And there's so many options with the Fiero.. like torque?  350 v8.. want revs?  quad 4 or 3.4 TDC.. lots of power but cheap on fuel?  series II 3800 S/C... high tech?  northstar.. just remember, you never know what's gonna be in the Fiero next to you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000046||Trapps||03-27-2001||09:59 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>I think he's trying to say.. "do you have any mods other than rims and exhaust?"...<P>I never have and never will be a fan of bubbly cars, or 4 door cars for that matter.  The contour is one of those, but I'm not saying it's slow or can't handle or whatever, it's just not what I like...  IMHO a "family car" like that just can't look good.  not flaming you, just expressing my opinion.<BR>And there is the fact that you can have a fully built Fiero (coilovers f&r, poly all around, big brakes, rims, built v6/v8 etc) for less than the cost of a contour, if you know what you're doing.  And there's so many options with the Fiero.. like torque?  350 v8.. want revs?  quad 4 or 3.4 TDC.. lots of power but cheap on fuel?  series II 3800 S/C... high tech?  northstar.. just remember, you never know what's gonna be in the Fiero next to you    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, more than meets the eye. custom intake (KKM, PRO Flow, Pro-M 75mm), computerized nitrous system (Venom VCN2000), springs (H&R's), y pipe (Shoshop), Short shifter (B&M), Oil, Fuel, Nitrous pressure guages (Autometer Phantoms), some minor cosmetic mods, and a Nakamichi & a/d/s sound sytem. I have two kids, it IS a family car. There isn't, last time I checked, room in a Fiero for the wife and two kids in car seats. I'd like a third (2 door) car, just no room in the budget right now.......<P>As I previously mentioned - I see the occasioanl V8 shoehorned into a Fiero on Woodward Ave., looks like fun. I'll post info here when the track event (Milan / April) is set - I hope to see some of you there.....<P>Mark<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Trapps (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000047||Standard||03-27-2001||01:56 PM||||Ah, so that's what that KKM is that I kept seeing..  I put family car in quotes becaust it's not your typical grocery getter car.  Sounds like a very well done car.  Have any pics of the engine?  What's it run in the quarter?||||reg||1
Z||000048||Trapps||03-27-2001||02:18 PM||||KKM is a K&N cone type filter - there is an inverted cone inside which gets air fed from a vent in the fenderwell. The Pro M 75mm is the polished part, Pro Flow is the meter on top of the Pro M. Pic is pre N20. <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1204400&a=8883688&p=29146629&Sequence=0">  <P>1/4 was 14.88. Haven't been to the track with the nitrous yet. Should be fun, some SVT's running NOS have hit the mid to high 13's. I only plan to run the equivalent of a 75 shot. If I hit 13.999 I'll be very happy. <P>Mark<P>Terrybogin, seriously, what classifies my car, in your opinion, as rice?<BR>[This message has been edited by Trapps (edited 03-27-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Trapps (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000049||cjbaldw||03-27-2001||04:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>If Ford hadn't dropped the SVT Contour, I would probably own one by now. I have a friend who asked me to do some work on his Contour, and I was really impressed with how it was designed and put together. <BR>I refuse to be a part of the <BR>"Ford sucks!" <BR>"No. GM sucks!" <BR>"No. Honda sucks!" argument.<BR>Most folks preferences are based upon what they know how to work on.<BR>And, I might add, <I>anything</I> can be modded to the point of absolute uselessness with the careful application of enough bad taste and money.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Later<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with you <B>completely</B>, well said...<P><P>------------------<BR>Regards,<P>Craig J. Baldwin<BR>99 SVT Contour - Silver - #49/2760 - ES Front Motor Mount Inserts, Bosche +4's w/Magnecore 8.5mm Competition wires, RActive Racing Pedals, KKM Intake/Pro-M 75mm MAF||||reg||14
Z||000050||cjbaldw||03-27-2001||04:36 PM||||Hey Mark/Trapps,<P>Nice piks my friend.  Sounds like u've done quite a bit to your SVT.  I'm not near as far along mods-wise, I'm basically stock.  As the parts degrade (like exhaust) I'm replacing w/aftermarket stuff.<P>I drive a new 4 door for two major reasons.  One, I have three kids and a loving wife at home, so I need the flexibility, and like Mark, don't wanna spend the $$ on a third car right now (although the Vette I'm thinking about seriously - see earlier posts in this thread).  Two, I wanted a newer car b/c I commute 100 miles a day to my office round trip and didn't want the hassle of maintaining an older vehicle, yet I wanted to drive something I rarely saw on the streets, and I don't see many SVT's at all driving around (Contours at least) because of their limited production runs.<P>Sounds like u Fiero guys have quite a few options on engines and whatnot, how do all of these different engines mate up with the drivetrain, I'd think this would present a problem in general??<P><P>------------------<BR>Regards,<P>Craig J. Baldwin<BR>99 SVT Contour - Silver - #49/2760 - ES Front Motor Mount Inserts, Bosche +4's w/Magnecore 8.5mm Competition wires, RActive Racing Pedals, KKM Intake/Pro-M 75mm MAF||||reg||14
Z||000051||Terrybogin||03-27-2001||08:06 PM||||I meant that the car was done in good taste, the Uncle Ben was just a wise crack. No, your car is not Rice. If it was a 4cyl LS with vinyl seats, manual windows, a sunroof that did not fit, wheels that made it look bolegged, springs making the car ride on the bumpstops, one huge tail pipe tip on a 1.5 inch exhaust system, a tri level wing with high altitude warning beacons (to keep helicopters from hitting it), misspelled characters in a language that no body understands, body trim in a color that has nothing to do with anything else on the car, sponsor stickers for products that are not even made for your make/model, and a Type-R or V-tec badge, then your car would be rice.||||reg||1
