Z||000053||p4n1c||03-27-2001||10:48 PM||||I wish Oldsmobile would release the OSVs, but that will never happen.  Stock supercharged 240hp engines(The Alero OSV is a <B>4cyl</B> 240hp supercharged). I would own one of those in a heartbeat.<P>Oh well, I will stick with the GM family(namely the Fiero).  To much blood, sweat and tears went into my parents Cutlass on behalf of my dad and me and it's still on the road after 401,000kms.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||9
Z||000054||Standard||03-28-2001||12:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cjbaldw:<BR><B>Sounds like u Fiero guys have quite a few options on engines and whatnot, how do all of these different engines mate up with the drivetrain, I'd think this would present a problem in general??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Any of the 60* V6's (3.1,3.4,3.4TDC) bolt right up to the existing tranny.  V8's need an adapter plate.  For the 3800 and quad 4 most people use the tranny's that were mated to the engines originally.  Just about any FWD tranny will fit in the Fiero engine compartment, along with the engine that comes with it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
